            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00117-010-2113-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 80-year-old male patient presented with acute chest pain. Clinically an aortic dissection or pulmonary embolism was suspected therefore non-ECG-gated multislice computed tomography was performed and despite the lacking ECG gating the causative high grade coronary stenosis could be identified.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
